TC ID	Test Case Title	Preconditions	Test Steps	Expected Result
TC_001	
Verify that the user can register a device-bound passkey using biometrics and then sign in successfully with it (end to end)
Connect ID is active and has no passkey registered. Device has a screen lock configured. Biometrics (fingerprint / face) are enrolled on the device.
1. Open the UAP page.
2. Enter the Connect ID.
3. Enter the password.
4. Click the Sign in button.
5. On the OTP page, enter the correct OTP.
6. Click Submit.
7. On the create passkey prompt, choose to create a passkey.
8. On the OS passkey prompt, verify with biometrics.
9. Sign out of UAP.
10. Open the UAP page and choose to sign in with the passkey for the Connect ID.
11. On the OS passkey prompt, verify with biometrics.
1. The create passkey prompt is displayed after OTP submission.
2. The passkey is created and a success confirmation is shown.
3. The user signs in with the passkey using biometrics and lands on the UAP home page.
